  "measurement_note": "Size is U, the number of distinct points in the completed reachable closure. Each tier starts from the eight corners of [0,m]^3 for m = 1, 2, and 3, so U is exactly 8, 27, and 64. The legal target [6,6,6] lies outside every closure, forcing stabilization. Incremental frontier simulation with hash-set membership processes each unordered reachable pair once in O(U^2) time. A correct list-based control explicitly scans its known points to detect every duplicate, takes O(U^3) time, completes all tiers, and should be rejected only by scaling.",
